1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,212
Hey!

2
00:00:01,162 --> 00:00:14,425
I'm Tirth, and I'm a college student who's genuinely tired of watching people struggle with the same boring, overloaded revision notes before board exams and competitive exams like JEE.

3
00:00:14,425 --> 00:00:18,762
So I'm building something different — it's called RevisionReel.

4
00:00:18,762 --> 00:00:30,787
Think of it like scrolling through Instagram, except every card teaches you one Physics, Chemistry, or Math concept in under a minute, with a quick quiz to lock it in.

5
00:00:30,787 --> 00:00:35,675
And here's the twist — I'm building this entire thing using AI.

6
00:00:35,675 --> 00:00:38,662
Not just a little bit of help.

7
00:00:38,662 --> 00:00:51,937
I'm talking full planning, full coding, full design — all done through AI tools, and I'm filming the whole process so you can actually see how it's built, bug by bug, decision by decision.

8
00:00:51,937 --> 00:00:56,050
This isn't a polished "look what I made" video.

9
00:00:56,050 --> 00:01:10,487
This is the real, messy, behind-the-scenes process — because I think more students need to see that building something real with AI is actually possible, even if you're still learning to code yourself.

10
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:22,862
Over the next few episodes, I'll show you the planning, the actual building, the bugs that break things, and eventually — a live app you can actually use to revise for your exams.

11
00:01:22,862 --> 00:01:26,712
If that sounds useful to you, follow along.

12
00:01:26,712 --> 00:01:35,562
Episode 2 is coming — where I break down exactly why revision the old way is broken, and what I'm doing differently.

